From: Michael R Sweet <msweet@msweet.org>
Date: Fri, 12 Jun 2026 19:43:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Sanitize destination-uri and pre-dial-string values
 (CVE-2026-55467)

Backport of upstream OpenPrinting/cups commit
0cf4e7814d6810ed3c454222bce3aa342d541681 (2.4.x, master equivalent
a9e7e7a3; upstream parent d41cf0616 = the quote_string fix carried by
backport-sanitize-backend-ipp-attr-strings.patch) - CVE-2026-55467:
the fax phone/faxPrefix options derived from a job's destination-uris
collection (destination-uri "tel:..." and pre-dial-string) bypassed the
CVE-2026-34980 control-character sanitizer, letting a print client
smuggle control characters (CR/LF) into the option string handed to the
fax backend (option-string grammar injection / incomplete-fix bypass).

Fix: copy both values through a control-char filter (<0x20 and DEL ->
space) into a bounded 256-byte buffer before cupsAddOption(), matching
upstream verbatim.

Product note: no fax queue is deployed in this product (CUPS_PRINTER_FAX
branch not exercised); carried to complete the 8d0f51ca sanitizer family
and keep the code line aligned with upstream 2.4.x.

Adaptation: none needed - context is byte-identical in this port's build
state (verified with git apply --fuzz=0 over the full install.py chain).

Upstream-commit: 0cf4e7814d6810ed3c454222bce3aa342d541681
Upstream-commit: a9e7e7a3a (master equivalent)
CVE: CVE-2026-55467
GHSA: GHSA-69qc-prxg-h2c7

diff --git a/scheduler/job.c b/scheduler/job.c
index 67b21513..eedd2a28 100644
--- a/scheduler/job.c
+++ b/scheduler/job.c
@@ -3952,12 +3952,37 @@ get_options(cupsd_job_t *job,		/* I - Job */
     ipp_t *ipp = ippGetCollection(attr, 0);	// Collection value
     const char *destination_uri = ippGetString(ippFindAttribute(ipp, "destination-uri", IPP_TAG_URI), 0, NULL);
     const char *pre_dial_string = ippGetString(ippFindAttribute(ipp, "pre-dial-string", IPP_TAG_TEXT), 0, NULL);
+    char buffer[256], *bufptr;		// Sanitized value
 
     if (destination_uri && !strncmp(destination_uri, "tel:", 4))
-      num_pwgppds = cupsAddOption("phone", destination_uri + 4, num_pwgppds, &pwgppds);
+    {
+      for (destination_uri += 4, bufptr = buffer; *destination_uri && bufptr < (buffer + sizeof(buffer) - 1); destination_uri ++)
+      {
+        if ((*destination_uri & 255) < ' ' || *destination_uri == 127)
+          *bufptr++ = ' ';
+	else
+	  *bufptr++ = *destination_uri;
+      }
+
+      *bufptr = '\0';
+
+      num_pwgppds = cupsAddOption("phone", buffer, num_pwgppds, &pwgppds);
+    }
 
     if (pre_dial_string)
-      num_pwgppds = cupsAddOption("faxPrefix", pre_dial_string, num_pwgppds, &pwgppds);
+    {
+      for (bufptr = buffer; *pre_dial_string && bufptr < (buffer + sizeof(buffer) - 1); pre_dial_string ++)
+      {
+        if ((*pre_dial_string & 255) < ' ' || *pre_dial_string == 127)
+          *bufptr++ = ' ';
+	else
+	  *bufptr++ = *pre_dial_string;
+      }
+
+      *bufptr = '\0';
+
+      num_pwgppds = cupsAddOption("faxPrefix", buffer, num_pwgppds, &pwgppds);
+    }
   }
 
  /*
